<title>USA: FGIC qualifies five muni bond issues for insurance.</title>
<headline>FGIC qualifies five muni bond issues for insurance.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-12-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Financial Guaranty Insurance Co said Wednesday it qualified for bond insurance the following five municipal issues scheduled for competitive sale today:</p>
<p>--Los Angeles Harbor Department, $320 million revenue bonds.</p>
<p>--West Haven, Conn., $7 million general obligation bonds.</p>
<p>--Windham, Conn., $21.945 million GOs.</p>
<p>--Clifton Board of Education, N.J., $15.3 million school bonds.</p>
<p>--Richland County School District No 1, S.C., $60 million GOs.</p>
<p>--U.S. Municipal Desk, 212-859-1650</p>
</text>
